4/ NFT and ETH depositors divide ETH PNL and FWA rewards according to a defined ratio, currently set at 90:10 in favor of ETH. This can and will be adjusted to promote pool balance as time goes on.

3/ The FWAPHouse aims to achieve both: depositors can deposit NFTs, ETH, or both, which get matched and listed in FWA at the pools configured backing (currently 0.06 ETH).

A keeper manages recycling the positions in perpetuity, with all PNL shared among depositors.

2/ The highest EV move in FWA is obviously holding the crown.

The second highest is to deposit NFTs with the minimum configured backing, or slightly above it when accounting for gas.

The problem is that it requires management to maximize returns, and scale to smooth them.

6/ The beauty of building on a permissionless blockchain is that anybody can build on top of your work.

This was a fun build, with lots of edge cases to account for.

Next up: something a little...bigger.

There's a teaser for that hidden for those who can find it.

